A transfer moves ``Money`` to a card its maker registered (the number is
sealed under the maker's own key, with a blind index). The maker confirms
it for its amount and card with a second factor (SCA); it counts against
the maker's limits in its own transaction; and one over the approval
threshold waits for another person, who steps up, to approve it. Requests
that move money carry an ``Idempotency-Key``.
